      <h2 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-prose mx-auto text-xl text-gray-500">
        If you can't find what you're looking for, you can always <a href="mailto:support@searchapi.io" class="font-medium text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-500">send us an email</a> with your enquiry.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-20">
      <dl class="space-y-10 lg:space-y-0 lg:grid lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-x-8 lg:gap-y-10">
          <div itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
            <dt itemprop="name">
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-900">Are failed request charges applicable?</h3>
            </dt>
            <dd class="mt-3 text-gray-500" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
              <span itemprop="text">We believe in charging only for successful outcomes. Therefore, you won't be billed for failed requests. Only successful searches with a 200 status code incur charges.</span>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
            <dt itemprop="name">
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-900">How fast does the SearchAPI deliver results?</h3>
            </dt>
            <dd class="mt-3 text-gray-500" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
              <span itemprop="text">Experience lightning-fast results! With our SearchAPI, you'll receive real-time data in mere seconds.</span>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
            <dt itemprop="name">
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-900">Is the API capable of handling large-scale requests?</h3>
            </dt>
            <dd class="mt-3 text-gray-500" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
              <span itemprop="text">With a robust foundation on the Amazon AWS cloud, we process millions of requests daily. Our extensive global proxy network of over 20 million, constantly benchmarked and rotated, ensures optimum performance and scalability.</span>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
            <dt itemprop="name">
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-900">What&#39;s the process for canceling a subscription plan?</h3>
            </dt>
            <dd class="mt-3 text-gray-500" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
              <span itemprop="text">Cancellation is hassle-free! Access your dashboard and terminate your plan in under 30 seconds.</span>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
            <dt itemprop="name">
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-900">Do you offer plans tailored to specific needs?</h3>
            </dt>
            <dd class="mt-3 text-gray-500" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
              <span itemprop="text">Of course! Recognizing the diverse needs of businesses, we're open to discussions for custom plans. Please contact us to craft a plan that aligns with your objectives.</span>
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div itemprop="mainEntity" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
            <dt itemprop="name">
              <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-900">Are there any rate limitations when using the SearchAPI?</h3>
            </dt>
            <dd class="mt-3 text-gray-500" itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
              <span itemprop="text">To maintain fairness and server integrity, there's a rate limit in place. Please note that you can utilize only up to 20% of your plan's credits each hour.</span>
            </dd>
          </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


